+      "title": "OpenTelemetry GenAI span instrumentation for LLM pipeline tracing",
+      "priority": "high",
+      "description": "Rainbow's traces config stores spans in the DB (backend: db) but does not emit structured OpenTelemetry spans conforming to the GenAI Semantic Conventions (v1.37+). Without standard spans, the system cannot be connected to any OTEL-compatible backend (Grafana, Datadog, Jaeger) for latency analysis, cost attribution per provider, or cross-request tracing. Adding OTEL instrumentation using the GenAI semantic conventions would give observable, interoperable telemetry without changing the existing DB trace store.",
+      "acceptanceCriteria": [
+        "Each AI provider call emits an OTEL CLIENT span with gen_ai.system, gen_ai.request.model, gen_ai.usage.input_tokens, gen_ai.usage.output_tokens, and gen_ai.response.finish_reasons attributes",
+        "Span name follows the format '{gen_ai.operation.name} {gen_ai.request.model}'",
+        "An OTEL exporter endpoint is configurable via OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT env var; when unset, traces are no-op (no external dependency)",
+        "Provider fallover spans are linked via trace context so the full retry chain is visible as a single trace",
+        "Promptfoo evals can optionally emit spans for eval runs"
+      ],
