-      "title": "Multi-turn LLM evaluation harness with simulated guest conversations",
+      "id": "US-999",
+      "title": "AI provider cost allocation by conversation type and profile",
       "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Research published in 2025 (Langfuse, OpenEvals) establishes that multi-turn chatbot systems should be evaluated by simulating complete conversations with a user simulator, then scoring the full conversation using LLM-as-a-Judge. Rainbow AI currently has Vitest unit tests for individual tools and Promptfoo for single-turn prompt evals, but no automated harness that simulates a 5-10 turn ordering or check-in conversation end-to-end and scores accuracy, context retention, and task completion.",
+      "description": "Rainbow runs multiple profiles (pelangi hostel, southern homestay, makan moments cafe) across many AI providers with per-provider cost budgets. The current cost tracking aggregates token usage across all profiles and conversation types, making it impossible to see which profile or intent category is driving AI spend. Breaking down costs by profile, conversation type (hostel booking vs. F&B order vs. general query), and provider gives management the data needed to optimise provider selection per use case and set tighter per-profile budgets.",
       "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A Promptfoo test suite contains at least 10 multi-turn conversation scenarios covering: order placement, order modification, out-of-stock handling, special instruction capture, and hostel check-in",
-        "Each scenario is scored on: task_completed (boolean), context_retained (0-1), and hallucination_free (0-1) using an LLM-as-a-Judge evaluator",
-        "The harness runs in CI (GitHub Actions) on every PR touching assistant/ or tools/ directories",
-        "A regression threshold alerts if average task_completed drops below 0.85 across all scenarios"
+        "Every AI provider call records profile_id and intent_category alongside token counts and computed cost",
+        "Admin cost dashboard shows a breakdown table: profile x intent_category x provider with daily/monthly token counts and USD cost",
+        "Per-profile daily budget cap can be configured independently (extending existing costBudget.providerBudgets)",
+        "An export endpoint returns cost breakdown data as CSV for the selected date range",
+        "Budget alert threshold alerts are evaluated per profile, not only globally"
       ],
       "technicalNotes": [
