-      "id": "US-1033",
-      "title": "Multi-agent inbox: assign and hand off conversations between Rainbow AI and human agents",
+      "id": "US-1001",
+      "title": "Drizzle ORM row-level security enforcement for tenant_id columns",
       "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Currently Rainbow AI handles all conversations autonomously; staff cannot interject or claim a conversation without the guest re-initiating. A human-takeover and reassignment flow is needed for complex or escalated cases, allowing staff to view the live queue, claim a conversation, respond manually, and return it to AI mode.",
+      "description": "Rainbow supports multiple profiles that share the same PostgreSQL database, but tenant isolation currently relies on application-layer filtering (WHERE profile_id = ?). If a query forgets the profile_id filter — a common developer error — data from one profile leaks into another. Enabling PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS) on all tenant-scoped tables and setting a runtime app.current_tenant variable before each query provides a defence-in-depth guard that enforces isolation at the database layer, complementing but not replacing the application-layer filters.",
       "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Staff can view a live queue of active AI-handled conversations in the admin panel",
-        "A 'Take over' button pauses AI auto-replies for that conversation and assigns it to the staff member",
-        "The guest receives a seamless transition message (e.g. 'You are now speaking with our team.')",
-        "Staff can return the conversation to AI mode after resolving the issue",
-        "Escalation events are logged in `escalation_events` with agent ID, timestamp, and reason",
-        "Conversation assignment is visible to all online agents to avoid double-handling"
+        "RLS is enabled on rainbow_conversations, rainbow_messages, intent_analytics, and escalation_events tables",
+        "A RLS policy enforces profile_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant') on all SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE operations",
