+      "id": "US-1021",
+      "title": "Multi-turn LLM evaluation harness with simulated guest conversations",
       "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Malaysia's first dedicated AI legislation is expected to be tabled to Cabinet in June 2026, using a risk-based framework developed by the National AI Office (NAIO). The bill will mandate harm assessment, incident reporting for AI-related harms, and full-lifecycle governance. Rainbow AI makes automated decisions affecting guests (booking eligibility, escalation routing, complaint handling) that will require documented risk classification and a structured incident log, distinct from the existing cultural bias audit stories.",
+      "description": "Research published in 2025 (Langfuse, OpenEvals) establishes that multi-turn chatbot systems should be evaluated by simulating complete conversations with a user simulator, then scoring the full conversation using LLM-as-a-Judge. Rainbow AI currently has Vitest unit tests for individual tools and Promptfoo for single-turn prompt evals, but no automated harness that simulates a 5-10 turn ordering or check-in conversation end-to-end and scores accuracy, context retention, and task completion.",
       "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "A risk classification document categorises each Rainbow AI automated decision type (booking, routing, pricing, escalation) by harm potential level (low/limited/high) aligned with the NAIO draft framework.",
-        "An AI incident log records all cases where the AI produced a response that led to a customer complaint, escalation, or admin override, with timestamp and resolution notes.",
-        "The admin dashboard includes an AI Incidents view with date-range filtering and CSV export.",
-        "A documented human-in-the-loop escalation path is tested for each high-risk decision type (e.g. booking refusal, price discrepancy)."
+        "A Promptfoo test suite contains at least 10 multi-turn conversation scenarios covering: order placement, order modification, out-of-stock handling, special instruction capture, and hostel check-in",
+        "Each scenario is scored on: task_completed (boolean), context_retained (0-1), and hallucination_free (0-1) using an LLM-as-a-Judge evaluator",
+        "The harness runs in CI (GitHub Actions) on every PR touching assistant/ or tools/ directories",
+        "A regression threshold alerts if average task_completed drops below 0.85 across all scenarios"
       ],
       "technicalNotes": [
-        "Malaysia NAIO risk-based framework aligns with EU AI Act tiering — Rainbow AI likely falls in limited risk for hospitality, but automated pricing or booking refusal may be high risk.",
-        "The existing escalation_events table in shared/schema-tables.ts is the foundation; add ai_incident_type and resolution_notes columns.",
-        "Distinct from Malaysia AI Governance 2024: fairness and cultural bias audit (BM/EN/ZH bias) — this story is legal compliance readiness for the incoming Act.",
-        "Reference: https://themalaysianreserve.com/2025/07/03/malaysia-targets-ai-law-by-2026-as-govt-weighs-risks-and-rules/"
+        "Langfuse supports multi-turn simulation via its dataset and experiment features",
+        "Promptfoo supports multi-turn test cases with the turns[] array in test case YAML",
