-      "id": "US-1047",
-      "title": "WCAG 3.0 draft preparation: cognitive accessibility and single-idea message splitting",
+      "id": "US-1022",
+      "title": "Proactive post-stay WhatsApp review request via utility template",
       "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "WCAG 3.0 (September 2025 W3C Working Draft) replaces binary pass/fail with a 0-4 scored outcome model and introduces specific outcomes for cognitive disability including Single Idea (one concept per message) and reading-level requirements. The Makan Moments webchat widget currently renders multi-sentence compound AI responses as a single bubble, which fails the WCAG 3.0 Single Idea outcome and makes responses harder for users with cognitive disabilities.",
+      "description": "Post-stay review solicitation is a proven pattern for hospitality chatbots. Under the July 2025 pricing model, a utility template sent within 24 hours of checkout (as a transaction follow-up) is free within the customer service window. No existing story covers automating a post-checkout review request (Google, Booking.com, or Airbnb) sent via WhatsApp 2-4 hours after checkout, triggered by the check-out event from the POS or booking system.",
       "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "AI responses containing more than one distinct idea or instruction are split into sequential chat bubbles (max one idea per bubble) in the webchat widget renderer.",
-        "All static UI text in the webchat widget reads at Flesch-Kincaid Grade 8 or below, verified by an automated readability check at build time.",
-        "A WCAG 3.0 outcome scoring baseline report is produced covering all draft outcomes applicable to chat interfaces, with scores 0-4 per outcome.",
-        "The webchat widget input accepts voice input via the browser Web Speech API as an alternative to text typing."
+        "A configurable post-checkout delay (default: 2 hours) triggers a WhatsApp utility template message to the guest's JID with a review request link (configurable per profile)",
+        "The trigger integrates with the existing POS webhook receiver or can be manually fired from admin UI per booking",
+        "If the guest has already rated 4+ stars via in-chat CSAT, the review request is suppressed to avoid duplication",
+        "Opt-out guests (tracked by existing opt-out story) never receive the message",
+        "Send volume and link click-through rate are tracked in analytics"
       ],
